    "title": "Person of interest sought in attempted arson at nightclub - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt McGovern No media credit provided. ,\n8 hours ago COLLEGE STATION, Texas ( FOX 44 ) – The College Station Police Department and Fire Marshals need your help to identify a person of interest in a case of attempted arson.\nPolice say the individual has curly hair, glasses, and a half-sleeve tattoo. He was captured on surveillance video inside of a local nightclub. The pictures below are courtesy of the College Station Police Department.\nThe person of interest entered the kitchen area, turned on multiple gas burners, successfully ignited one of the stoves, and opened a CO₂ tank before leaving. The nightclub was filled with hundreds of patrons at the time of this incident, making his actions especially dangerous.\nIf you recognize this individual or have any information on this case, you can contact the College Station Police Department at 979-764-3600 and reference Case #2025-006659.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KWKT - FOX 44.",
